     kkbbdd is used to change the keyboard encoding.  The encoding is set to na‐
     tional keyboard layout _n_a_m_e, and a short message is printed to stdout.

     The execution of kkbbdd normally occurs in the system multi-user initializa‐
     tion file _/_e_t_c_/_r_c using the encoding defined in _/_e_t_c_/_k_b_d_t_y_p_e.

     The options are as follows:

     --ll      List all available keyboard encodings.

     --qq      Quiet mode.  No message is printed unless an error occurs.

